From: Michael Knopke <knopkem@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:21:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Dummy renderer: Make RID owners thread-safe

RID_Alloc only locks its mutex when the owner is declared with
THREAD_SAFE = true. The dummy renderer's owners were all declared
without it, so concurrent RID allocation from multiple threads raced
and could hand out the same RID twice, corrupting resources.

This can happen whenever resources are created from worker threads in
headless mode (e.g. threaded resource loading or threaded imports),
which the threaded scene import now exercises heavily.
---
 servers/rendering/dummy/storage/light_storage.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/servers/rendering/dummy/storage/light_storage.h b/servers/rendering/dummy/storage/light_storage.h
index 6be1c0b1..50eb6ec3 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/dummy/storage/light_storage.h
+++ b/servers/rendering/dummy/storage/light_storage.h
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ private:
 		RID lightmap;
 	};
 
-	mutable RID_Owner<LightmapInstance> lightmap_instance_owner;
+	mutable RID_Owner<LightmapInstance, true> lightmap_instance_owner;
 
 public:
 	static LightStorage *get_singleton();
